WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:00.733
 

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.668
CESAR: When I started my
journey and people started

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.370
calling me the Dog Whisperer,

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:06.339
the only thing I wanted to
do is to teach people there is

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:08.374
no such a thing as a bad dog.

00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:09.408
WOMAN: Oh, my gosh.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:12.779
CESAR: Give me the leash.
She's safer with me.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.081
Today, I'm still
doing what I love,

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:16.582
but the world has changed.

00:00:16.615 --> 00:00:18.584
(overlapping chatter)

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:22.221
CESAR: Record dog adoptions
have made many packs complete.

00:00:22.254 --> 00:00:26.325
But now more than ever,
people and dogs still...

00:00:26.358 --> 00:00:27.326
Tsch.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:28.327
Need...

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.328
Tsch.

00:00:29.361 --> 00:00:30.229
Help.

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:31.230
WOMAN: We can't live like this.
MAN: Yeah.

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:32.197
WOMAN: The problem is me.
MAN: What do I do?

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:34.467
CESAR: More pooches,
more problems, right?

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.135
He needs rehab like ASAP.

00:00:36.168 --> 00:00:37.837
So many things you
can fix already.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.038
Tsch!

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:39.972
MARLON: Sorry, I'm sorry.
CESAR: Ignore the excitement.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:40.907
MEGAN: I just don't
want you to get bit.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.810
CESAR: Do you know who I am?
MEGAN: Yes.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.478
CESAR: Together
with my superhero pack,

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:48.448
our mission is to teach the
world to honor the pack code,

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:51.217
honesty, integrity, and loyalty.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.586
Once you get this, you're
going to have everything else.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:54.587
ALL: Yay!

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.489
CESAR: And that's how we
create better humans and

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:59.125
better dogs one pack at a time.

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:05.131
When a dog bite his own human,
one bite is too many.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:07.633
But when a dog makes a habit
of attacking his own people,

00:01:07.666 --> 00:01:10.270
that makes it a
red zone behavior.

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.806
Today, I'm going to Anaheim to
meet this French Bulldog whose

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:17.210
territorial aggression can
get so bad that the family

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.312
sometimes have
to hide from him.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:22.148
It's like being
prisoners in their own home.

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:29.222
PRISCILLA: I am
Priscilla Serrano.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.590
My dog's name is Jax.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.558
He's two years old.

00:01:32.591 --> 00:01:35.428
And he is a French Bulldog.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:39.165
I was just going Christmas
shopping one day, I saw him,

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:41.167
and I literally fell in love.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.303
I was like, "Ooh, this is my
dog, like I feel the connection.

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:46.339
I'm taking him home."

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:49.275
You're so cute.

00:01:49.441 --> 00:01:52.278
DANIEL: I'm Daniel.
I'm Priscilla's boyfriend.

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:54.747
So I guess that makes
me Jax's stepfather.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.285
He's a very sweet, loving dog.

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:03.623
PRISCILLA: Whenever he's with
me, he cuddles up next to me

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.726
and he kisses my face and
shakes his little tail.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:10.196
He gets excited, like, you can
see that there's love there,

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.498
that he has love in his heart
for each and every person

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:14.467
in this home.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.903
It's just he has
unpredictable behavior.

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.204
(growling)

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:19.805
Hey, down.

00:02:19.838 --> 00:02:21.541
(barking)

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.244
DANIEL: He does have
outbursts and they're scary.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.546
(barking)

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:32.752
Jax has bitten me four times,
in the knee, hand, and again.

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:36.722
PRISCILLA: I am grateful to be
still living with my parents

00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:39.759
and he's actually attacked
my mom multiple times.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.495
He nipped her underneath
her chin pretty bad.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:45.965
My grandmother unfortunately
one time tried playing with him,

00:02:45.998 --> 00:02:49.302
grabbed a toy,
and he got at her hand.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.338
ISAIAH: Seeing him bite my
grandma, my mom, and, like,

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.807
I'm in my room hearing them
scream and stuff about it,

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.276
like, that's where
I'm, like, really scared.

00:02:57.309 --> 00:03:00.246
And I would definitely say
that Jax is a lost cause.

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:02.215
AMY: I am afraid of Jax.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:05.318
My mother-in-law, she's
definitely scared of him.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.721
I don't wanna be on,
everybody on edge.

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:10.289
ISAIAH: It's like
walking on eggshells.

00:03:10.322 --> 00:03:12.625
PRISCILLA: Jax's behavior
has really affected my

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:14.827
relationship with my family.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:18.598
Before, my parents would come
into my room and hang out with

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:22.468
me and now it's
not even an option.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:25.304
Sit. Sit.

00:03:25.337 --> 00:03:27.340
Life with Jax is exhausting.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:32.545
I've come to a point
where I feel like I
don't know what to do.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:36.382
It's been a year of this
behavior and I don't wanna

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:39.452
imagine how long
this can go for.

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:44.824
The worst-case scenario
would be him getting at

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.760
my grandmother or my mom,
my boyfriend, my brother,

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:51.631
to a point of, like, no return.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.433
I hate to say it, it breaks
my heart to say it,

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:55.868
it makes me emotional to say it.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:59.505
But my only option
would be to put him down.

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:03.843
I'm sorry.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:10.683
Family to me means being there
for each other, not giving up

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:12.818
on each other.

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:16.422
In my heart, I
can't give up on Jax.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.627
I need Cesar's help right now.

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:31.837
CESAR This guy is keeping
the whole family prisoner,

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.474
so let's find out what the
root of the problem is.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.343
(doorbell, knocking)

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.513
PRISCILLA: Hi.
DANIEL: Hi.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:41.514
CESAR: Come on out, guys.
Come on out.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:42.482
PRISCILLA: Thank you.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:43.316
How are you? Thank you
so much for being here.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:44.750
CESAR: Really good.
Danny, right?

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:45.617
DANIEL: Yes, sir.

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:46.452
CESAR: Priscilla.
Nice to meet you.

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:47.453
PRISCILLA: Very
nice to meet you.

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:48.888
DANIEL: Nice to meet you.
CESAR: Un placer.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:49.789
So how can I help you?

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.724
PRISCILLA: So we got
Jax two years ago.

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:52.692
CESAR: Okay.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:54.093
PRISCILLA: And after he
turned a year was when

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:55.728
the behavior really started.

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:57.196
CESAR: Uh-hmm.

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:59.465
PRISCILLA: It started
off where he became
very territorial of toys.

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:00.366
CESAR: Okay.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.535
PRISCILLA: Then it
was areas in the house.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.003
CESAR: Okay.
PRISCILLA: Me.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.137
CESAR: Okay.

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:07.073
PRISCILLA: And now it
seems like it's just anything.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.441
DANIEL: He's really
good outside the house.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.575
PRISCILLA: Yeah.

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:10.977
CESAR: So it's about the family.
He's against the family.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.546
DANIEL: It feels like it.
It does. It really does
feel like it.

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:16.882
PRISCILLA: It feels genuinely.
He's bitten my mom.

00:05:16.915 --> 00:05:18.918
DANIEL: He got me right
here a couple days ago.

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:19.886
CESAR: Ooh.

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.554
PRISCILLA: But he has
bitten my abuelita and.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.856
CESAR: He bit grandma?
PRISCILLA: Uh-hmm.

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:25.791
CESAR: It's an absolute must
that Priscilla's family feels

00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:28.527
safe in their own house.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.632
So Jax attacking grandma,
mom, and Danny is an
immediate call to action.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:35.067
It's innate in dogs
to protect their pack.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:39.806
So Jax turning on his pack
tells me he's very confused.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.941
PRISCILLA: I believe that this
opportunity came to me for a

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.943
reason and I
genuinely believe that.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.845
CESAR: Yeah.
Well, we gotta work hard.

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.546
That's it.

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:49.448
So this is what I'm gonna do,
I'm gonna go in the backyard,

00:05:49.481 --> 00:05:50.783
we're gonna put
some cameras inside.

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:52.852
I wanna see the behavior,
see what you do.

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:55.554
I just wanna do it without
my energy influencing Jax.

00:05:55.587 --> 00:05:56.455
PRISCILLA: Thank you.
CESAR: All right.

00:05:56.488 --> 00:05:58.591
I'll go this way,
you guys go inside.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:01.160
 NARRATOR: While Cesar
 monitors from outside,
 Danny and Priscilla

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:04.931
 head to her room, a place Jax
 often behaves aggressively.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:07.900
PRISCILLA: Sit.
DANIEL: Hi, babas.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:10.035
PRISCILLA: Oh, who is that?
DANIEL: Hi, babas.

00:06:10.068 --> 00:06:11.070
No.

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:17.510
(barking)

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.011
CESAR: This dog is confused.

00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:21.147
Right away, this
guy wants to fight.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.748
Yeah, super confused.

00:06:22.781 --> 00:06:29.055
(barking)

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:32.024
CESAR: Aggression is
never the problem, it's
the outcome of a problem.

00:06:32.057 --> 00:06:35.895
So the confusion is terrible.

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:38.164
DANIEL: Calm down.
Hey. It's okay.

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:42.101
CESAR: Ooh.
Saying okay is not okay.

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:44.203
The dog doesn't feel good, so
don't say okay when the dog

00:06:44.236 --> 00:06:46.605
doesn't feel good.

00:06:46.638 --> 00:06:47.807
This dog is
absolutely confused.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.508
DANIEL: Hey, hey. Jax.

00:06:49.541 --> 00:06:50.743
(snapping)

00:06:50.776 --> 00:06:52.645
No.

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:55.014
CESAR: Priscilla and Danny
are giving Jax mixed signals.

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:58.017
First, they tell him no
but then they say it's okay.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.052
That is super
confusing for a dog.

00:07:00.085 --> 00:07:02.688
And when a dog is constantly
confused like Jax,

00:07:02.721 --> 00:07:06.959
his instincts can tell
him to fight or flight.

00:07:06.992 --> 00:07:09.495
It is pretty clear
what Jax has chosen.

00:07:09.528 --> 00:07:11.630
DANIEL: If I come here to
grab like a food bowl...

00:07:11.663 --> 00:07:13.466
(barking)

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:14.533
donezo.

00:07:14.566 --> 00:07:15.467
PRISCILLA: No.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:16.235
DANIEL: He's completely
blind right now too.

00:07:16.268 --> 00:07:18.504
PRISCILLA: He's gone.
Stop it.

00:07:18.537 --> 00:07:20.873
DANIEL: He was,
just pure anger.

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:22.708
(barking)

00:07:22.741 --> 00:07:24.944
I mean, I've seen him mad, I
mean he's, he's bitten me a

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:28.214
couple times and especially
recently I thought it was

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:31.584
never gonna get
worse than how it was.

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:35.588
To see him push that,
it was intense.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.723
PRISCILLA: It was scary.
It was terrifying.

00:07:37.756 --> 00:07:41.861
No. No. No!

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:45.498
CESAR: This is bad
obviously because he's,
he's in a red zone.

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:48.033
He's gonna hurt, he's gonna
bite anything that gets near it.

00:07:48.066 --> 00:07:50.603
PRISCILLA: Come. Come.

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.805
CESAR: Ooh.
She's frustrated.

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.774
She doesn't wanna deal with
him, so she's just putting him

00:07:55.807 --> 00:07:56.809
in the crate.

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.878
(snarling)

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:02.681
They're clueless.
I gotta stop this right now.

00:08:02.714 --> 00:08:05.618
Big no no for the dog people.

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.720
Never force a
dog into the cage.

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:09.321
Never trap a dog in a cage.

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:12.057
Instead, you treat him like
a regular dog, you treat
him like a wild animal.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.860
Those are where
aggression comes from.

00:08:14.893 --> 00:08:16.028
Right?

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:17.930
And then they take this
reaction against anybody that

00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:20.766
is not the person that put him
in, because he's not gonna do

00:08:20.799 --> 00:08:24.136
it towards Priscilla but he
will do it to everybody else.

00:08:24.169 --> 00:08:26.705
Okay. I just need
something to protect me.

00:08:26.738 --> 00:08:30.643
Once I know that a
dog bites or lunges,
normally I grab something.

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:33.179
I'm just protecting myself.

00:08:33.845 --> 00:08:36.282
(barking)

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:37.917
DANIEL: Hey, Jax.
PRISCILLA: No.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.084
CESAR: Don't, don't
let that bother you.

00:08:39.117 --> 00:08:40.619
He can't see you right now.

00:08:40.652 --> 00:08:41.587
DANIEL: Right.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.989
CESAR: He's literally
blinded by the rage.

00:08:44.022 --> 00:08:47.593
So this is not territory,
this is beyond territory.

00:08:47.826 --> 00:08:49.194
We need to get him
out of the crate.

00:08:49.227 --> 00:08:50.729
He could hurt
himself in there.

00:08:50.762 --> 00:08:54.267
This mindset in the
crate is dangerous.

00:08:57.069 --> 00:09:02.008
(barking)

00:09:02.141 --> 00:09:05.044
What we're dealing with is this
is the animal, the animal,

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:06.345
(barking)

00:09:06.378 --> 00:09:07.713
you wanna be able to open this.

00:09:07.746 --> 00:09:09.615
(barking)

00:09:09.648 --> 00:09:10.983
This is the danger zone.

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:13.752
This is definitely a
red, red, red zone.

00:09:13.785 --> 00:09:16.989
These kind of dogs can
actually hurt themselves and

00:09:17.022 --> 00:09:18.357
grab things and stay there.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.826
They don't mind to
kill themselves.

00:09:20.859 --> 00:09:22.795
DANIEL: No!
CESAR: Don't get angry.

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:24.296
If you get angry,
just breathe it out.

00:09:24.329 --> 00:09:26.031
You get frustrated,
just breathe it out.

00:09:26.064 --> 00:09:26.999
DANIEL: I know what you mean.
I'm like.

00:09:27.032 --> 00:09:28.867
CESAR: Yeah.
You get tense, breathe it out.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.001
DANIEL: Uh-hmm. Tense, yeah.

00:09:30.035 --> 00:09:33.072
PRISCILLA: Jax is out of
control and seeing how he is

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:36.742
with Cesar makes
me very worried.

00:09:36.775 --> 00:09:40.045
Maybe my dog,
like, can't be helped.

00:09:40.078 --> 00:09:41.680
CESAR: He's gonna get tired.

00:09:41.713 --> 00:09:43.015
As long as we have
the leash, we got him.

00:09:43.048 --> 00:09:49.155
(barking)

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:53.726
(barking)

00:09:53.759 --> 00:09:56.295
Hey. Hey. Come on.

00:09:56.428 --> 00:09:57.896
Shh.

00:09:57.929 --> 00:09:59.165
(barking)

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.769
(barking)

00:10:03.802 --> 00:10:07.840
CESAR: Tsch. (bleep).

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:09.375
We need the leash to keep
him from hurting himself.

00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:11.243
(exhales heavily)

00:10:14.312 --> 00:10:16.315
There you go.

00:10:16.348 --> 00:10:18.884
(deep breath)

00:10:18.917 --> 00:10:21.286
You put him away when he gets in
trouble and then you trap him.

00:10:21.319 --> 00:10:24.156
They don't understand
why you put him away.

00:10:24.189 --> 00:10:28.694
Hey. Tsch. Tsch.

00:10:31.763 --> 00:10:33.332
There we go.
Now he's calming back down.

00:10:33.365 --> 00:10:34.600
You see that?

00:10:34.633 --> 00:10:36.435
So now that he's relaxed, this
is when you can say he's okay.

00:10:36.468 --> 00:10:38.771
Not earlier when he was
trying to attack you.

00:10:38.804 --> 00:10:39.705
DANIEL: Right.

00:10:39.739 --> 00:10:41.774
CESAR: Here's what's
going on in this house.

00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:44.376
Have you heard the
saying blind with rage?

00:10:44.409 --> 00:10:47.079
That is the next level of
aggression Jax is reaching.

00:10:47.112 --> 00:10:48.047
What's causing that?

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.849
Confusion, he doesn't
know if he's supposed to

00:10:50.882 --> 00:10:52.885
protect or attack his pack.

00:10:52.918 --> 00:10:55.721
No wonder the entire
family hides from him.

00:10:55.754 --> 00:10:58.457
Priscilla loves her dog but
she's afraid of his behavior.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:02.094
The dog feels that
fear and believes his
human is in danger.

00:11:02.127 --> 00:11:05.931
So he doubles down and charges
anyone who comes near his mom.

00:11:05.964 --> 00:11:08.867
This is a volatile mix
of aggression, fear, and

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.904
confusion that makes
Jax a red zone threat.

00:11:11.937 --> 00:11:14.707
And the only solution is
for Priscilla to wake up and

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:19.178
realize that it's her
fearful energy that is
causing Jax to lash out.

00:11:19.211 --> 00:11:21.180
You're used to your anxiety.

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:22.047
PRISCILLA: I am.

00:11:22.081 --> 00:11:23.182
CESAR: You have
learned to live with it.

00:11:23.215 --> 00:11:26.118
But fear is not allowed.
Otherwise, it's contagious.

00:11:26.151 --> 00:11:30.022
That's why I'm not bringing
you closer because I could
still see your anxiety.

00:11:30.055 --> 00:11:30.956
PRISCILLA: Yeah.

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:32.825
CESAR: I can still
see your uncertainty.

00:11:32.858 --> 00:11:34.960
If you were holding
the leash instead of me,

00:11:34.993 --> 00:11:36.995
he wouldn't be calm like this.

00:11:37.028 --> 00:11:40.866
I know it's hard.
But find a positive mindset.

00:11:40.899 --> 00:11:43.869
So every time you get nervous,
frustrated, anxious,

00:11:43.902 --> 00:11:45.938
just go back to calm confident,
love and joy,

00:11:45.971 --> 00:11:49.374
Do you think you will
be able to find confidence
within yourself?

00:11:49.407 --> 00:11:55.815
PRISCILLA: Not to, like, say
anything bad about my parents

00:11:56.081 --> 00:11:59.151
but I don't think they
ever instilled that in me.

00:12:00.886 --> 00:12:04.456
I know that progress is not
just a straight line going up.

00:12:04.489 --> 00:12:06.892
I know that sometimes
we fall back and.

00:12:06.925 --> 00:12:08.327
CESAR: That's right.

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:12.030
PRISCILLA: But I want
myself to get better.

00:12:12.063 --> 00:12:15.935
I'm going to get better.
So he's gonna get better.

00:12:17.836 --> 00:12:21.907
I never really had anyone to
kind of tell me how important

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:25.043
it is to have calm and
confidence and be joyful,

00:12:25.076 --> 00:12:27.112
no matter your circumstance.

00:12:27.145 --> 00:12:30.315
It made me feel something
I've just never felt before.

00:12:30.348 --> 00:12:33.319
And that gives me hope.

00:12:33.619 --> 00:12:34.987
CESAR: What I would like to
do for you guys is to continue

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.222
your learning, to
continue your growth.

00:12:37.255 --> 00:12:40.058
I want you guys to come to the
DPC, my ranch. Thank you.

00:12:40.091 --> 00:12:41.093
DANIEL: Thank you.

00:12:44.429 --> 00:12:46.198
PRISCILLA: Thank you so much.
CESAR: Con la familia!

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:51.904
 NARRATOR: The next day,
 Priscilla, Danny, and Jax

00:12:51.937 --> 00:12:54.807
 arrive at the
 Dog Psychology Center.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:57.309
DANIEL: We really gotta
make sure this works, babe.

00:12:59.511 --> 00:13:02.247
 NARRATOR: The dog's
 rehabilitation is
 even more urgent.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:05.050
 Just this morning, Jax's
 behavior escalated to

00:13:05.083 --> 00:13:07.286
 a new level of aggression.

00:13:08.119 --> 00:13:09.855
CESAR: How's it going?

00:13:09.888 --> 00:13:13.292
PRISCILLA: He's still
just acting like just rage.

00:13:13.325 --> 00:13:15.594
I do feel like I don't have
control because for the

00:13:15.627 --> 00:13:18.263
first time ever, Jax
redirected on me.

00:13:18.296 --> 00:13:21.167
(growling)

00:13:21.367 --> 00:13:23.101
That's never happened before.

00:13:23.134 --> 00:13:25.370
DANIEL: This is as
serious as it's gotten.

00:13:25.403 --> 00:13:26.638
PRISCILLA: Uh-hmm.

00:13:26.671 --> 00:13:30.008
He jumped at me, growled, and
tried to bite, like, it was an

00:13:30.041 --> 00:13:32.144
attempt to actually attack me.

00:13:32.177 --> 00:13:33.479
CESAR: It's a
dangerous confusion.

00:13:33.512 --> 00:13:36.582
He needs to learn not
to feel threatened when
someone guides him.

00:13:36.615 --> 00:13:39.117
Jax had been very
confused for a long time.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:41.954
And now anything
can trigger him.

00:13:41.987 --> 00:13:44.122
He reminds me of
The Incredible Hulk.

00:13:44.155 --> 00:13:47.125
You don't know when
he's gonna turn green.

00:13:47.158 --> 00:13:49.595
(growling)

00:13:49.628 --> 00:13:51.997
Ah-ha! I got it.

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:53.465
(barking)

00:13:53.498 --> 00:13:55.634
In his confused mind,
he's in charge.

00:13:55.667 --> 00:13:59.438
So he acts aggressive when he
feels his power is challenged,

00:13:59.471 --> 00:14:02.074
like Priscilla's
handling this morning.

00:14:02.107 --> 00:14:04.343
Yeah. Shh. Okay.

00:14:04.376 --> 00:14:06.111
So here, this is
just to protect.

00:14:06.144 --> 00:14:09.648
The first thing we must do is
to get him on a leash to show

00:14:09.681 --> 00:14:13.552
him how to behave when a calm,
confident human is in charge

00:14:13.585 --> 00:14:18.057
and that the crate cannot
be allowed as a trigger
for his aggression.

00:14:19.291 --> 00:14:25.497
(barking)

00:14:28.366 --> 00:14:31.303
There you go.

00:14:31.336 --> 00:14:34.106
Tsch. Hey. Tsch.

00:14:34.139 --> 00:14:36.575
See? My confidence is
calming him down.

00:14:36.608 --> 00:14:38.143
Tsch.

00:14:38.176 --> 00:14:43.549
So we remove him
then he goes back.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:49.154
And then erase the
bad impression, like
hitting a reset button.

00:14:49.387 --> 00:14:52.324
We're eliminating the
first picture that we got.

00:14:52.357 --> 00:14:54.359
DANIEL: Oh.
CESAR: Yeah.

00:14:54.392 --> 00:14:57.563
So now with me, the crate is
starting to equal calmness.

00:14:57.763 --> 00:14:59.031
Tsch.

00:14:59.064 --> 00:15:02.001
Stay.

00:15:02.568 --> 00:15:04.670
PRISCILLA: Baby, are
you nervous right now?

00:15:04.703 --> 00:15:05.704
DANIEL: It's, I'm surprised.

00:15:05.737 --> 00:15:06.838
CESAR: No, he's surprised.

00:15:06.872 --> 00:15:09.341
Yeah, if a guy does this,
he's like, "Oh, (bleep)"!

00:15:09.374 --> 00:15:11.410
PRISCILLA: He really
snapped him out that quickly.

00:15:11.443 --> 00:15:15.314
So that was really amazing
to see, because I didn't even

00:15:15.347 --> 00:15:17.683
realize we're doing it wrong.

00:15:17.716 --> 00:15:20.052
You know, that's what's
Cesar is teaching us.

00:15:20.085 --> 00:15:20.886
CESAR: Come on.
PRISCILLA: Yay.

00:15:20.919 --> 00:15:22.054
DANIEL: Okay.
CESAR: Follow me, guys.

00:15:22.087 --> 00:15:25.424
Today's first exercise is a
two for one special, which

00:15:25.457 --> 00:15:28.026
will help build Priscilla's
confidence while also

00:15:28.059 --> 00:15:29.695
addressing Jax's confusion.

00:15:29.728 --> 00:15:32.331
And specifically his negative
reaction when Priscilla

00:15:32.364 --> 00:15:34.299
puts him in the crate.

00:15:34.332 --> 00:15:36.969
Watch. Here.
Right here.

00:15:37.002 --> 00:15:38.971
Just grab the leash and
ask him to follow you.

00:15:39.004 --> 00:15:40.138
Boom, boom, boom, boom.

00:15:40.171 --> 00:15:41.206
Come on, come on.

00:15:41.239 --> 00:15:44.476
And then once
you come here, go.

00:15:44.509 --> 00:15:46.979
Yeah. You see?

00:15:47.012 --> 00:15:48.113
Like a bowling ball.

00:15:48.147 --> 00:15:50.182
That ball had to go exactly
where you want it to go.

00:15:50.215 --> 00:15:53.218
And now you can see he's in
there and calm because I took

00:15:53.251 --> 00:15:55.520
control of him with
the right energy.

00:15:55.553 --> 00:15:56.754
PRISCILLA: Okay.
CESAR: You understand?

00:15:56.788 --> 00:16:00.993
So you are conditioning the
brain to accept your direction

00:16:01.026 --> 00:16:03.528
while also telling him
he's safe in the crate.

00:16:03.561 --> 00:16:05.063
PRISCILLA: Okay.
CESAR: Okay.

00:16:05.096 --> 00:16:06.698
PRISCILLA: Okay.
CESAR: All right, Priscilla.

00:16:06.731 --> 00:16:11.236
I want like a
cheerleader but a coach.

00:16:11.402 --> 00:16:13.638
This is gonna build
so much trust, guys.

00:16:13.671 --> 00:16:16.108
Just remember
happy-go-lucky, Priscilla.

00:16:16.141 --> 00:16:18.043
PRISCILLA: Come on, come on.
CESAR: Right next to it.

00:16:18.076 --> 00:16:19.277
PRISCILLA: Come on. Come on.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:21.380
CESAR: Be confident.
Lead him.

00:16:21.413 --> 00:16:24.483
PRISCILLA: Come on. Come on.

00:16:24.683 --> 00:16:26.318
No. Don't jump off.

00:16:26.351 --> 00:16:27.652
CESAR: Be careful.
You're too far in front.

00:16:27.685 --> 00:16:31.790
PRISCILLA: Okay.
Come. You got it.

00:16:31.823 --> 00:16:33.458
CESAR: Not like that.
Don't hesitate.

00:16:33.491 --> 00:16:34.692
PRISCILLA: Come on.

00:16:34.726 --> 00:16:36.528
CESAR: So that hesitation, we
don't want it on the crate.

00:16:36.561 --> 00:16:40.532
PRISCILLA: Come on.
Come on. Okay, ready.

00:16:40.565 --> 00:16:41.700
Come on. Come on.

00:16:41.733 --> 00:16:44.336
CESAR: Right from there.
PRISCILLA: Let's go. Let's go.

00:16:44.369 --> 00:16:45.470
CESAR: As soon as you see that
he's coming in, send him into

00:16:45.503 --> 00:16:48.407
the crate like a bowling ball.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:49.341
Go.

00:16:49.375 --> 00:16:52.778
PRISCILLA: Come on.
Come on. Hey. Back.

00:16:52.811 --> 00:16:54.079
CESAR: Don't force him.

00:16:54.112 --> 00:16:56.481
PRISCILLA: Come on.
Come on.

00:16:56.514 --> 00:16:59.018
CESAR: It's not working.
Let's do it again.

00:16:59.852 --> 00:17:03.255
Nobody wants to be pushed into
something they are not sure of.

00:17:03.288 --> 00:17:07.192
So jacking the leash is
only going to confuse
and anger him again.

00:17:07.458 --> 00:17:10.228
She needs to use the motion
and confident energy to create

00:17:10.261 --> 00:17:13.799
a momentum that guides
the dog into the crate.

00:17:13.832 --> 00:17:15.534
PRISCILLA: Let's go.
Let's go.

00:17:15.567 --> 00:17:16.768
CESAR: Come back.
PRISCILLA: Come on.

00:17:16.802 --> 00:17:19.271
CESAR: And then, and then two,
three feet away from the crate.

00:17:19.304 --> 00:17:20.806
PRISCILLA: Go in the crate.

00:17:20.839 --> 00:17:24.142
CESAR: Yup. Stay.
PRISCILLA: Wait.

00:17:24.175 --> 00:17:26.478
CESAR: Don't let him move.

00:17:27.178 --> 00:17:29.581
Then bring it out.
Come on.

00:17:29.614 --> 00:17:31.216
Celebrate, celebrate,
celebrate. Yay.

00:17:31.249 --> 00:17:32.818
(cheering)

00:17:32.851 --> 00:17:34.853
Priscilla did better the
second time around but she

00:17:34.886 --> 00:17:37.255
still have a long way to go.

00:17:37.288 --> 00:17:39.791
She's really going to have to
practice overcoming her fear

00:17:39.824 --> 00:17:43.295
and claiming her leadership
position in the pack if she

00:17:43.328 --> 00:17:45.597
ever wants Jax to respect her.

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:49.568
He doesn't take you serious in
the leader aspect because in

00:17:49.601 --> 00:17:51.369
the beginning, you hesitated.

00:17:51.402 --> 00:17:53.605
Your calm, confident
energy wasn't strong enough.

00:17:53.638 --> 00:17:54.873
PRISCILLA: Okay.

00:17:54.906 --> 00:17:56.808
CESAR: He's only gonna follow if
your energy is calm, confident.

00:17:56.841 --> 00:17:58.777
PRISCILLA: Okay.
CESAR: Not fearful.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:17:59.978
PRISCILLA: Okay.

00:18:00.011 --> 00:18:01.480
CESAR: And the more he lives
with a fearful energy you've

00:18:01.513 --> 00:18:05.617
been giving him, the
harder it's going to be
to get him rehabilitated.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:06.785
PRISCILLA: Uh-hmm.
CESAR: Jax.

00:18:06.818 --> 00:18:08.420
(barking, snarling)

00:18:11.923 --> 00:18:13.225
CESAR: Tsch. Tsch.

00:18:13.258 --> 00:18:15.460
(barking, snarling)

00:18:15.493 --> 00:18:19.531
I got it.
Tsch. Tsch. Tsch.

00:18:20.665 --> 00:18:24.436
Luckily, he didn't get me but
I need to lay him on his side

00:18:24.469 --> 00:18:25.737
until he fully surrenders.

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:27.439
DANIEL: Yup.
CESAR: Tsch.

00:18:27.472 --> 00:18:33.678
(barking)

00:18:33.711 --> 00:18:35.380
Tsch.

00:18:35.413 --> 00:18:36.715
There you go.

00:18:36.748 --> 00:18:38.383
DANIEL: It's exactly
what I'm telling you
is that, like, yeah.

00:18:38.416 --> 00:18:39.718
PRISCILLA: It's
out of nowhere.

00:18:39.751 --> 00:18:41.219
CESAR: He has an episode.

00:18:41.252 --> 00:18:42.521
DANIEL: Is it done?
Is my question.

00:18:42.554 --> 00:18:43.722
CESAR: Not yet.

00:18:43.755 --> 00:18:46.224
He's still dealing with all
the tension that he built up

00:18:46.257 --> 00:18:49.361
with that outburst but
eventually, he'll let it out.

00:18:49.394 --> 00:18:50.595
He's gonna go...

00:18:50.628 --> 00:18:52.831
(sigh)

00:18:52.864 --> 00:18:55.634
so by them doing that
is they're breathing

00:18:55.667 --> 00:18:57.536
that tension away from them.

00:18:57.569 --> 00:19:01.840
PRISCILLA: Ohhh-kay.

00:19:01.873 --> 00:19:03.742
CESAR: Just wait for it.

00:19:03.775 --> 00:19:05.510
Boom. Look.

00:19:05.543 --> 00:19:07.312
And then he wakes up
like it's nothing.

00:19:07.345 --> 00:19:10.549
Like he just woke
up from a dream.

00:19:10.582 --> 00:19:12.751
But still, I don't like that
he's acting out like that.

00:19:12.784 --> 00:19:14.853
Where does this
aggression come from?

00:19:14.886 --> 00:19:17.355
Well, Jax was doing
well with the exercise.

00:19:17.388 --> 00:19:18.790
PRISCILLA: Go in the crate.
CESAR: Yup.

00:19:18.823 --> 00:19:21.393
But remember, this
is day one of rehab.

00:19:21.426 --> 00:19:24.362
And he's been living like
The Hulk for a long time.

00:19:24.395 --> 00:19:27.666
So anything can trigger him
and I am ready for moments of

00:19:27.699 --> 00:19:29.434
aggression like this.

00:19:29.467 --> 00:19:32.571
I'll address his angry Hulk
outburst until eventually he

00:19:32.604 --> 00:19:35.807
learns the most important
lesson in this rehab.

00:19:36.207 --> 00:19:39.644
He must stop attacking his
pack or else his family might

00:19:39.677 --> 00:19:42.247
feel forced to put him down.

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:45.283
This intensive level of
rehab can only be achieved by

00:19:45.316 --> 00:19:47.852
keeping him here at the DPC.

00:19:47.885 --> 00:19:50.722
My next suggestion is
for him to stay with us.

00:19:50.755 --> 00:19:52.290
PRISCILLA: Yes. Okay.

00:19:52.323 --> 00:19:53.458
CESAR: He's not
ready to go home.

00:19:53.491 --> 00:19:54.526
PRISCILLA: Uh-hmm.

00:19:54.559 --> 00:19:57.262
I think this is a good
reset for him, for myself.

00:19:57.295 --> 00:19:59.731
I mean, he just redirected on
me and I think this is a good

00:19:59.764 --> 00:20:01.733
break that we all need.

00:20:01.766 --> 00:20:03.868
CESAR: Use this time to
work out or meditate,

00:20:03.901 --> 00:20:05.804
whatever makes you
feel calm, confident.

00:20:05.837 --> 00:20:06.705
PRISCILLA: Okay.

00:20:06.738 --> 00:20:08.006
CESAR: So he will
see you as a leader.

00:20:08.039 --> 00:20:08.873
PRISCILLA: Yes.

00:20:08.907 --> 00:20:10.976
CESAR: You need to
gain the respect.

00:20:11.009 --> 00:20:12.344
PRISCILLA: Okay.
DANIEL: Yeah.

00:20:12.377 --> 00:20:13.478
CESAR: All right.
DANIEL: Yeah.

00:20:13.511 --> 00:20:15.013
CESAR: Jax. Come on.

00:20:15.046 --> 00:20:17.816
Let's go say bye.
Let's walk him out.

00:20:20.051 --> 00:20:21.386
 NARRATOR: The next morning.

00:20:21.419 --> 00:20:22.654
CESAR: Unleash the hounds.

00:20:22.687 --> 00:20:25.357
 NARRATOR: Cesar assembles
 his dogs for the morning hike.

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:27.392
(barking)

00:20:27.425 --> 00:20:29.695
CESAR: Come on.

00:20:30.362 --> 00:20:33.031
 NARRATOR: But Jax's continued
 confusion prevents him from

00:20:33.064 --> 00:20:35.667
 even following a
 simple pack walk.

00:20:36.734 --> 00:20:38.837
CESAR: Jax,
where are you going?

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:39.671
Look.

00:20:39.704 --> 00:20:41.773
He does, look, he
just takes off.

00:20:41.806 --> 00:20:43.541
See how the pack gathers?

00:20:43.574 --> 00:20:44.675
Yeah.

00:20:44.709 --> 00:20:46.845
If the pack goes this way,
he should follow the pack.

00:20:46.878 --> 00:20:48.980
He doesn't know how to
stay within the group.

00:20:49.013 --> 00:20:50.515
He's not connected.

00:20:50.548 --> 00:20:53.418
So he has no understanding
to stay within the pack.

00:20:53.451 --> 00:20:55.353
He just goes. Look.

00:20:55.386 --> 00:20:57.922
When we brought a troubled dog
here at the DPC, I want them

00:20:57.955 --> 00:21:00.659
to switch into a
balanced pack mindset.

00:21:00.692 --> 00:21:04.863
But Jax is still so
confused that I need to
try something drastic.

00:21:04.896 --> 00:21:07.899
Using an item that he has such
a negative association with,

00:21:07.932 --> 00:21:10.835
I wanna give him a
positive experience.

00:21:10.868 --> 00:21:13.305
(whistling, smooches)

00:21:13.338 --> 00:21:15.006
There you are.

00:21:15.039 --> 00:21:16.508
We're throwing a crate party.

00:21:16.541 --> 00:21:18.310
Let's continue with the rehab.

00:21:18.343 --> 00:21:21.379
(clapping)

00:21:21.412 --> 00:21:22.981
I'm gonna show you how the
pack is gonna help him to

00:21:23.014 --> 00:21:25.884
associate the crate in a
completely different way.

00:21:25.917 --> 00:21:28.586
The pack will be his
role models, which creates a

00:21:28.619 --> 00:21:31.923
stronger connection to
both my dogs and me.

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:36.795
Look, he knows this is
his crate by the way.

00:21:36.828 --> 00:21:37.963
This is his crate.

00:21:37.996 --> 00:21:41.333
As we all remember the last
time I was near the crate,

00:21:41.366 --> 00:21:45.070
I need to use a racket,
you know, just to block him.

00:21:45.103 --> 00:21:47.639
Because, you know, The Hulk
was coming out.

00:21:47.672 --> 00:21:50.475
For Jax, the crate
equals confusion.

00:21:50.508 --> 00:21:53.445
It represents fear for
both him and his mom.

00:21:53.478 --> 00:21:55.714
In his mind, he's being
trapped so he behaves

00:21:55.747 --> 00:21:57.482
like a wild animal.

00:21:57.515 --> 00:22:00.919
It is a constant trigger that
turns Jax into the angry Hulk.

00:22:00.952 --> 00:22:03.555
My dogs will use their
happy-go-lucky energy to show

00:22:03.588 --> 00:22:06.858
Jax the crate is not
something to fear.

00:22:08.559 --> 00:22:10.495
It's good that he's not
charging or lunging but you

00:22:10.528 --> 00:22:12.931
can definitely
see he's unsettled.

00:22:12.964 --> 00:22:15.867
Come on. Come on. Come on.

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:17.502
(smooches)

00:22:18.236 --> 00:22:20.405
He's a, he's a
little bit guarding it.

00:22:20.438 --> 00:22:24.376
He's not as relaxed as the
rest of the pack, you know?

00:22:24.409 --> 00:22:26.444
Good girl, Sophia.

00:22:26.477 --> 00:22:28.012
He's the only one not getting
the food yet because he's a

00:22:28.045 --> 00:22:31.649
little bit tense, because his
association of the crate,

00:22:31.682 --> 00:22:36.087
I mean, he's going in there but
